  "description": "Spacious One-Bed with Own Door and Large Private Patio\n\nAn excellently presented bright, well-presented one-bedroom apartment with its own front door, set in the heart of Grand Canal Dock. It has a generous open-plan lounge and dining area, and floor-to-ceiling glazing opens onto a large private patio, which is rare for a city-centre apartment.\n\nThe finer details \nOwn-door access\nLarge open-plan lounge with a comfortable sofa and armchair, and warm timber flooring throughout\nDining area with a glass table and seating for four\nFloor-to-ceiling windows with blinds, opening onto a large private patio overlooking the landscaped courtyard and water feature\nFitted kitchen with granite worktops, electric oven, hob, extractor, microwave and toaster\nDouble bedroom with [wardrobes / en suite, if applicable]\nBathroom with [bath / shower]\n[Furnished / unfurnished]\n[Parking / bike storage / bin facilities / management details]\n\nThe patio is ideal for morning coffee, summer evenings, or working outside when the weather allows.\n\nLocation and local amenities\nHanover Quay is one of Dublin's most sought-after addresses. It's a vibrant, safe and well-serviced docklands neighbourhood, a short walk from the city centre.\n\nCulture and leisure\n\nBord Gáis Energy Theatre, with West End shows, concerts and ballet\nGrand Canal Square, with its open-air events, red-carpet plaza and light installation\n3Arena and the Aviva Stadium, within easy reach for concerts and sport\nConvention Centre Dublin\nWalks along the waterfront, the Grand Canal Dock basin and the Samuel Beckett Bridge\n\nFood, drink and daily needs\n\nA wide choice of cafés, restaurants, bars and takeaways around Grand Canal Square, Hanover Quay and Sir John Rogerson's Quay\nThe Marker Hotel and its rooftop bar\nConvenience stores, supermarkets, pharmacies and gyms close by [name your nearest]\n\nTransport\n\nGrand Canal Dock DART station, with direct access along the coast\nPearse Street DART station and the Luas at Spencer Dock, a short walk away\nDublin Bus routes at the nearby stops, including the 60, 52, 82, C1, 27 and 56a, plus the 84n Nitelink\nWalkable to St Stephen's Green, Grafton Street, Trinity College and Merrion Square in about 15 to 20 minutes\nExcellent cycling routes, and straightforward access to the M50 and Dublin Airport\n\nWork and green space\n\nWithin walking distance of the Silicon Docks, including the Dublin offices of Google, Meta, TikTok and Airbnb, as well as the IFSC and many other employers\nNearby parks and open spaces, plus Sandymount Strand and the Irishtown Nature Reserve a short distance away",
